How loop and break work in Rust: a loop can hand a value back out with break value. Rust Day 12 of the Zero to Pro series.

📌 In this short:
✅ loop { } repeats forever until you break out of it
✅ break counter * 2; returns a value from the loop: let result = loop { ... };
✅ continue skips the rest of this pass; a while loop always gives back () (error E0308): only loop can break with a value

💻 Code from the video:
let mut counter = 0;
let result = loop {
    counter += 1;
    if counter == 10 {
        break counter * 2;
    }
};
println!("{result}"); // 20

📖 Learn more: https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/ch03-05-control-flow.html
